<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Le Moyne d&apos;Iberville asked for a same-day visit for a painful lump on his right forearm. Five days ago a splinter of oak went into the skin while he was inspecting timber in the dockyard; he pulled it out. Three days ago the spot became red and sore, and since yesterday it has swollen into a tender lump that throbs at night. He has had no fever, chills or sweats, and he checked his temperature twice a day as his fever card asks. No red streaks up the arm. He has had no earlier skin infections and no one at home has boils. He takes no regular medicines. He asked whether he needs antibiotics. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Three days ago, after a splinter five days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Back of the right forearm</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Three days</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Throbbing, tender lump</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>4 of 10</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Constant, worse at night</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Wood splinter in the dockyard; recent malaria treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Warm compresses helped a little</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>No fever or chills; no red streaks</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

